+   published by script (`--card-pad-t`, `--card-foot-h`, `--masthead-foot`, `--pin-band`, the
+   motion rungs) carries an `@property` registration with an `initial-value`, and consumers
+   then write `var(--x)` with NO fallback — so an absent publisher fails at computed-value
+   time and a born-RED row that deletes the publisher catches it, instead of a `, 0px` that
+   quietly paints a wrong-but-plausible layout. §10's LEADER (CTRL-FACE, taking TAPE's) lands that block
+   once, for the whole wave.
